#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:30
#: 144ab860f4b4438ba513fe5b64297efb
msgid "For firmware versions prior to 4.5, autopilots with an IOMCU co-processor (e.g. Pixhawk, CubeOrange,etc.) the DShot ESCs should be connected to the AUX outputs and not the MAIN outputs of the IOMCU co-processor. In firmware versions 4.5 or later, the :ref:`BRD_IO_DSHOT<BRD_IO_DSHOT>` parameter may be set to load Dshot compatible IOMCU firmware on the next boot-up for some autopilots using F103 IOMCUs. If this parameter is not present, then the autopilot does not have DShot capability on its IOMCU outoputs. See the :ref:`IOMCU Dshot Limitations <iomcu-dshot>` section for limitations and more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:32
#: c1aad124540f47d68a3cf16fac550679
msgid "On CubeOrange DShot works on all channels.  AUX1 cannot be used for Bi-Directional DShot meaning only AUX2 to AUX6 can be used for Bi_directional DShot.  (`see issue <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/20362>`__)."
